EXPLANATION :PCB Drafting and Manufacturing Documentation – THEJAS32-Based FPV FCNS
1. Introduction

The PCB drafting document represents the engineering drawing and manufacturing information for the THEJAS32-Based FPV Flight Control and Navigation System (FCNS).

The document provides a visual representation of the PCB assembly, a Bill of Materials (BOM), a realistic 3D view of the board, and a drill table containing the hole sizes and quantities required for manufacturing.

PCB drafting is an important stage of hardware development because it connects the electronic circuit design with the physical manufacturing process. The schematic defines the electrical connections, the PCB layout defines component placement and copper routing, and the drafting document presents important design information in a form that can be reviewed before fabrication and assembly.

The main purposes of this document are:

To present the physical arrangement of PCB components.
To document the electronic components used in the design.
To provide a 3D representation of the assembled PCB.
To document the drilling requirements for manufacturing.
To support mechanical inspection and component-placement verification.
To provide a reference for PCB fabrication, assembly, and future maintenance.
