3. Top-Side PCB View

The top-side PCB view shows the board from above, including the positions and orientations of the electronic components.

The main controller is positioned near the center of the board, with supporting components and connectors arranged around it.

This view is useful for understanding the overall component-placement strategy.

Purpose of the top-side view

Component identification:
The view helps identify component locations using their designators, such as U5, U6, U7, J1, and other reference labels.

Placement verification:
It helps check whether components are placed in their intended positions and orientations.

Connector accessibility:
The locations of external connectors can be reviewed to ensure that cables and programming interfaces can be accessed.

Mechanical inspection:
The positions of components relative to the board edges and mounting holes can be inspected.

Assembly reference:
The top-side view can help during PCB assembly, troubleshooting, and visual inspection.

For this FPV flight controller, suitable component placement is important because the board integrates processing, motion sensing, power conversion, and external communication interfaces within a compact area.

Design consideration: The top-side view provides placement information, but electrical connectivity must be verified using the schematic and PCB net information.

