5. Bill of Materials (BOM)

The Bill of Materials is a list of the electronic components required to assemble the PCB.

The BOM in the drafting document contains component designators, descriptions or part numbers, and quantities.

Each component has a reference designator that identifies its position in the circuit design.

For example:

U5 identifies the THEJAS32 controller.
U6 identifies the ICM-42688-P motion sensor.
U7 identifies the BMI270 motion sensor.
U4 identifies the DPS310 barometric sensor.
U2 identifies the CH340C USB-to-serial interface.
U3 identifies the W25Q128-family external flash device shown in the BOM.

These reference designators allow the schematic, PCB layout, BOM, and assembly documentation to be related to one another.

